Hardcoded Serial Modules
------------------------

These modules are hardcoded to work with a card in a specific slot: this is to
enable cards which don't agree with the host machine (eg: old serial port issue
1 or 2 serial cards in a RiscPC) to be used. It may be necessary to remove the
ROM from the card to make the machine boot. To use, simply load the appropriate
module in your boot sequence (put it in !Boot.Choices.Boot.Predesk folder).

Serial port issue 1 card (Natsemi 16C552, 44 pin PLCC)   Iss1_SlotX
Serial port issue 2/3 card (Exar 16C552, 68 pin PLCC)	 Iss2_SlotX

Atomwide issue 1/2 cards work fine in RiscPCs already, so modules for these
cards are not supplied.

